# Git_Golden_Questions (Scenario Based) (0–3 Years DevOps Engineer)

These are real Git scenarios…

Frequently asked in DevOps interviews 👇

---

## 1. You committed wrong code. How will you undo it?

* Not pushed:

```bash
git reset --soft HEAD~1
git reset --mixed HEAD~1
git reset --hard HEAD~1
```

* Already pushed:

```bash
git revert <commit_id>
```

---

## 2. You pushed to the wrong branch. What will you do?

```bash
git checkout correct-branch
git cherry-pick <commit_id>
git checkout wrong-branch
git reset --hard HEAD~1
git push --force
```

---

## 3. Merge conflict occurred. How will you resolve it?

* Open file → resolve conflict markers

```bash
git add .
git commit
```

---

## 4. You want to undo last commit but keep changes. How?

```bash
git reset --soft HEAD~1
```

---

## 5. You want to discard local changes completely. What will you do?

```bash
git reset --hard
git clean -fd
```

---

## 6. You need to temporarily save changes without committing. How?

```bash
git stash
git stash pop
```

---

## 7. Your local branch is behind remote. How will you sync?

```bash
git pull
# or
git fetch
git rebase origin/branch-name
```

---

## 8. You accidentally deleted a branch. Can you recover it?

```bash
git reflog
git checkout -b recovered-branch <commit_id>
```

---

## 9. You want to revert a pushed commit. How will you do it?

```bash
git revert <commit_id>
```

---

## 10. You want to delete last commit permanently. How?

```bash
git reset --hard HEAD~1
git push --force
```

---

## 11. Multiple developers changed same file. How will Git handle it?

* Auto merge if different lines
* Conflict if same lines → manual resolution

---

## 12. You want to see changes before commit. Which command?

```bash
git status
git diff
git diff --staged
```

---

## 13. Commit history is messy. How will you clean it?

```bash
git rebase -i HEAD~n
```

---

## 14. You want to move commits to another branch. How?

```bash
git checkout target-branch
git cherry-pick <commit_id>
```

---

## 15. You need to ignore certain files. What will you use?

* `.gitignore` file

---

## 16. Your code is not updating after pull. Why?

* Wrong branch
* Local changes conflict
* Detached HEAD
* Remote not updated
* Need rebase

---

## 17. You want to compare two branches. How?

```bash
git diff branch1..branch2
```

---

## 18. You want to undo changes in a specific file. How?

```bash
git restore file.txt
```

---

## 19. Repository size is too large. What will you do?

* Remove large files
* Use Git LFS
* Clean history (BFG / filter-branch)

---

## 20. Credentials exposed in repo. What is your immediate action?

* Revoke credentials
* Rotate secrets
* Remove from history
* Force push cleaned repo
* Inform team

---

## 21. You want to apply specific commit to another branch. How?

```bash
git cherry-pick <commit_id>
```

---

## 22. You need to rename a branch. How?

```bash
git branch -m old-name new-name
git push origin new-name
git push origin --delete old-name
```

---

## 23. You want to squash multiple commits. How?

```bash
git rebase -i HEAD~n
```

---

## 24. Detached HEAD state. What does it mean?

* Not on any branch
* Working directly on commit

---

## 25. You want to restore deleted file. How?

```bash
git restore file.txt
```

---

## 26. Git push rejected. How will you fix it?

```bash
git pull --rebase
git push
```

---

## 27. You want to see who changed a line in file. How?

```bash
git blame file.txt
```

---

## 28. You want to clone specific branch only. How?

```bash
git clone -b branch-name --single-branch <repo-url>
```

---

## 29. Git stash not working as expected. Why?

* No changes to stash
* Untracked files not included

```bash
git stash -u
```

---

## 30. What is your step-by-step approach to handle Git issues in projects?

1. Check `git status`, `git log`, `git diff`
2. Verify branch
3. Take backup branch
4. Choose safe fix (prefer revert)
5. Resolve conflicts
6. Test locally
7. Push safely
8. Communicate with team

